@startuml state-ota-session
' State machine: one OTA update, as the host drives it.
'
' Grounded in real source:
'   - src/integration/OtaSession.cpp  (the Boost.SML transition table)
'   - src/integration/OtaSession.h    (OtaStage, OtaFailure)
'   - docs/adr/0034-ota-session-as-a-state-machine.md
'   - docs/protocols/uart-flash-v1.md (section 5 the steps, section 6 failures)
'
' Every arrow below is one row of that table, so the picture and the code
' cannot drift apart without the table changing.

title OTA update session - host side (OtaSession)

skinparam shadowing false

[*] --> Idle

Idle --> Probing : start / INFO_REQ
Idle --> Failed : start [image empty]

Probing --> Done : INFO [target version, confirmed]\nnothing to do
Probing --> Confirming : INFO [target version, on trial] / CONFIRM
Probing --> Beginning : INFO [other version] / BEGIN(size, CRC32, version)

Beginning --> Sending : ACK (bank erased) / DATA(offset 0)
Sending --> Sending : ACK [more image left] / DATA(next offset)
Sending --> Committing : ACK [all sent] / COMMIT
Committing --> Rebooting : ACK (banks switched, board resets)
Rebooting --> Rechecking : reboot wait elapsed / INFO_REQ
Rechecking --> Confirming : INFO [target version] / CONFIRM
Rechecking --> Failed : INFO [other version]\nWrongVersion
Confirming --> Done : ACK

state "any waiting state" as Waiting
Waiting --> Waiting : NAK BAD_CRC [resends left] / same frame again
Waiting --> Failed : NAK (any other code)\nBoardRefused
Waiting --> Waiting : timeout [resends left] / same frame again
Waiting --> Failed : timeout [budget spent]\nNoAnswer

Done --> [*]
Failed --> [*]

note right of Waiting
  Probing, Beginning, Sending, Committing,
  Rechecking and Confirming each list these
  four rows in the table, one per state, so
  the table says exactly which states accept
  which events.
end note

note bottom of Rebooting
  Nothing is sent into a board that is
  resetting. The wait is the only state with
  no frame in flight.
end note

note bottom of Failed
  An event no row accepts is a ProtocolError:
  the table is the whole contract, so a frame
  that does not belong here stops the session
  instead of passing quietly.
end note

@enduml
